From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:38:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Tell the port when the V-blank work is done (SDK_PORT_3DS)

After V-blank the game updates the display for the next picture: screen
fades, the V-blank callback (OAM, palettes, VRAM transfers, BG updates)
and the post-V-blank tasks. On the DS all of that happens before the
screen starts drawing the picture. The port draws the screens on other
threads, so it needs to know when the game is done: NitroPort_VBlankWorkDone
after the main loop's V-blank work, and after WaitFrame's.
---
 src/main.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main.c b/src/main.c
--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -35,6 +35,16 @@
 
 #define RESET_COMBO (PAD_BUTTON_START | PAD_BUTTON_SELECT | PAD_BUTTON_L | PAD_BUTTON_R)
 
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// The port draws the screens on other threads (other CPU cores on a 3DS),
+// from the registers, palettes, OAM and VRAM as they are. After V-blank the
+// game changes them all for the next picture (the V-blank callback, screen
+// fades, the post-V-blank tasks); on the DS that happens before the screen
+// starts drawing it. This tells the port when it's done, so a screen isn't
+// drawn halfway through (3ds_port/nitro/include/nitro_port.h).
+extern void NitroPort_VBlankWorkDone(void);
+#endif
+
 FS_EXTERN_OVERLAY(game_start);
 FS_EXTERN_OVERLAY(game_opening);
 
@@ -158,6 +168,9 @@ void NitroMain(void)
 
         SoundSystem_Tick();
         SysTaskManager_ExecuteTasks(gSystem.postVBlankTaskMgr);
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+        NitroPort_VBlankWorkDone();
+#endif
     }
 }
 
@@ -216,6 +229,9 @@ static void WaitFrame(void)
     if (gSystem.vblankCallback != NULL) {
         gSystem.vblankCallback(gSystem.vblankCallbackData);
     }
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+    NitroPort_VBlankWorkDone();
+#endif
 }
 
 static void TrySystemReset(enum OSResetParameter resetParam)
